      "title": "gospray - Simple LDAP bind-based password spray tool",
      "summary": "On a network and need credentials? Try password spraying the domain controller directly. A few years ago, I wrote this password spray tool called gospray that was used succesfully in a couple of engagements since. It does an LDAP bind directly against the domain controller to validate credentials. This doesn’t require an SMB server (or other servers) as target. So, it’s pretty quiet and number of concurrent Go routines is configurable. :)",
